### Nixpkgs version

- Stable (26.05)

### Describe the bug

With `boot.binfmt.emulatedSystems = [ "aarch64-linux" ];` active on an x86 system it is possible to build and switch into an ARM configuration (including an ARM bootloader). This system won't be able to boot and roll back any more, and has to be recovered with a live image.

### Steps to reproduce

1. have a system with x86 architecture with `boot.binfmt.emulatedSystems = [ "aarch64-linux" ]` set
2. `sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#my-aarch64-server` (forgetting `--target-host root@my-aarch64-server` by mistake); this will deploy the ARM server config onto the laptop and kill your desktop environment, forcing you to reboot
3. reboot
4. be unable to boot (see screenshot)

### Expected behaviour

There should be a switch inhibitor to prevent one from doing this.

### Screenshots

<img width="1280" height="800" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c7bb6104-9213-4a4f-b8ff-16adb9861572" />

### Additional context
This can be used to reproduce my issue. It will produce the above screenshot as build output.

```nix
let
  nixpkgs = builtins.fetchTarball "https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/archive/be29768cc24f309d77c467c4e099b9825d22a1b2.tar.gz";
  pkgs = import nixpkgs { system = "x86_64-linux"; };
  arm =
    (import "${nixpkgs}/nixos/lib/eval-config.nix" {
      modules = [
        {
          nixpkgs.hostPlatform = "aarch64-linux";
          boot.loader.systemd-boot.enable = true;
          fileSystems."/" = { device = "/dev/vda"; fsType = "ext4"; };
          system.stateVersion = "26.05";
        }
      ];
    }).config.system.build.toplevel;
in
pkgs.testers.runNixOSTest {
  name = "cpu-family-repro";
  nodes.machine = {
    virtualisation.useBootLoader = true;
    virtualisation.useEFIBoot = true;
    boot.loader.systemd-boot.enable = true;
    boot.binfmt.emulatedSystems = [ "aarch64-linux" ];
    virtualisation.additionalPaths = [ arm ];
  };
  testScript = ''
    machine.wait_for_unit("multi-user.target")
    machine.succeed("nix-env -p /nix/var/nix/profiles/system --set ${arm}")
    print(machine.execute("${arm}/bin/switch-to-configuration boot 2>&1")[1])
    print(machine.succeed("ls -R /boot/EFI; cat /boot/loader/loader.conf"))
    machine.shutdown()
    machine.start()
    machine.wait_for_console_text("No bootable option")
    machine.screenshot("broken")
    machine.crash()
  '';
}
```

